  "raw": {
    "https://jobs.gfcmsu.edu/postings/2589": {
      "title": "Dental Hygiene Faculty",
      "description": "Great Falls College Montana State University Employment Opportunities | Dental Hygiene Faculty Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Benefits HR Office GFCMSU HOME Choose Great Falls Dental Hygiene Faculty Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants must submit: Resume/CV Cover Letter Name, address, & phone # of 3 professional references Unofficial Transcripts License for dental hygiene with local anesthesia endorsement Position Details Position Information Working Title Dental Hygiene Faculty Brief Position Overview Great Falls College is seeking a qualified dental hygienist to join the Dental Hygiene program as a full-time faculty member. Faculty in this role will support student learning in classroom, laboratory, and clinical settings. This position is well suited for hygienists who are interested in teaching, mentoring, and strengthening the dental hygiene workforce in Montana. Faculty work collaboratively with colleagues to maintain accreditation standards, support student success, and ensure the curriculum reflects current professional practice. Faculty Tenure Track Yes Faculty Rank Tenure-Track Position Number Department Dental Hygiene Division Health Sciences Appointment Type Faculty Contract Term Academic Year Semester If other, specify From date If other, specify End date FLSA Union Affiliation Montana Two-Year College Faculty Association FTE 1.0 Benefits Eligible Yes Compensation Annual Salary $48,535-$58,561 commensurate with experience, education, and placement on the salary structure. Contract Type MUS If other, please specify Recruitment Type Open Position Details General Statement Great Falls College is seeking a qualified dental hygienist to join the Dental Hygiene program as a full-time faculty member. Faculty in this role will support student learning in classroom, laboratory, and clinical settings. This position is well suited for hygienists who are interested in teaching, mentoring, and strengthening the dental hygiene workforce in Montana. Faculty work collaboratively with colleagues to maintain accreditation standards, support student success, and ensure the curriculum reflects current professional practice. Why Teach at Great Falls College? Gorgeous Clinical Facility Work in our gorgeous, brand-new clinic, designed to support hands‑on learning using modern equipment and technologies that mirror real-world practice. Montana Lifestyle at Its Best Great Falls is centrally located with easy access to Yellowstone and Glacier National Parks, endless outdoor recreation, and the unique “Montana quality of life” that hygienists across the state know and love. Supportive, Collaborative Program Join a team of experienced faculty, engaged students, and strong community partners—all committed to delivering exceptional dental hygiene education. Meaningful Impact Across Montana Your expertise will help address workforce needs statewide, supporting healthier communities and empowering students to build fulfilling careers. What You Get as a GFC Employee Generous Benefits Package We contribute $1,080/month toward Medical, Dental, Vision, Life, and Long-Term Disability Insurance—supporting you and your family with comprehensive coverage. Full Health Insurance Options Choose from robust medical, dental, and vision plans that fit your needs and lifestyle. A Welcoming Community You’ll be joining a team that values work-life balance, professional growth, and the supportive, down-to-earth culture Montana is known for. Duties and Responsibilities Develop, teach, and assess didactic, laboratory and clinical classes using traditional and alternative delivery methods, as permitted by the faculty member’s current degree. Supervise and instruct students completing course and clinical requirements Advise students in the dental hygiene program Participate in college activities and committees beyond one’s discipline Regularly attend program meetings and collaborate with colleagues, within the department and across campus. Required Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills Bachelor’s degree in any field. Minimum of two years of clinical dental hygiene experience Demonstrates strong written, oral, electronic and interpersonal communication skills Demonstrates strong computer skills License to practice as a registered dental hygienist in Montana with a local anesthesia endorsement Preferred Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills Bachelor’s degree in dental hygiene from an accredited program Experience in teaching didactic and/or clinicals. The Successful Candidate Will Special Requirements This position is not eligible for sponsorship. This job description should not be construed as an exhaustive statement of duties, responsibilities or requirements, but a general description of the job. Physical Demands To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. The requirements listed above are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. The Program The Department The College Great Falls College is a 2-year institution in the Montana University System, dedicated to providing high quality, affordable education. Located in the heart of Montana, we offer more than 25 academic programs that prepare students for immediate employment or seamless transfer to four-year institutions. Our small class sizes, 8- and 16-week courses, dedicated faculty and vibrant learning community ensure students receive the personalized attention and support needed to succeed. Our non-credit workforce training programs provide practical skills and knowledge for in-demand careers, helping students enter the workforce or advance their careers with confidence. At Great Falls College, we believe in making education accessible to everyone. Our tuition is among the most affordable in Montana, and we offer financial aid options, scholarships, and dual credit opportunities to help students save on their educational journey. Join the River Otter team and help transform lives and shape the future of our community. This position has supervisory duties? Posting Detail Information Announcement Number FAC - VA - 2600003P Number of Vacancies Desired Start Date Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Close Date 10/29/2026 Open until filled Yes Special Instructions Summary Applicants must submit: Resume/CV Cover Letter Name, address, & phone # of 3 professional references Unofficial Transcripts License for dental hygiene with local anesthesia endorsement Quick Link for Internal Postings https://jobs.gfcmsu.edu/postings/2464 Notices Great Falls College Montana State University is committed to providing a working and learning environment free from discrimination. As such, the College does not discriminate in the admission, access to or conduct of its educational programs and activities nor in its employment policies and practices on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, ethnicity, creed, service in the uniformed services (as defined in state and federal law), veteran status, gender, age, political beliefs, marital or family status, pregnancy, physical or mental disability, genetic information, gender identity, gender expression, or sexual orientation or preference. In support of the College’s mission to be inclusive and diverse, applications from qualified minorities, women, veterans and persons with disabilities are highly encouraged. Great Falls College Montana State University makes accommodation for any known disability that may interfere with an applicant’s ability to compete in the hiring process or an employee’s ability to perform the duties of the job. In compliance with the Montana Veteran’s Employment Preference Act, GFC MSU provides preference in employment to veterans, disabled veterans, and certain eligible relatives of veterans. To claim veteran’s preference or request accommodation, contact the Human Resources Office, Great Falls College Montana State University, 2100 16th Ave S, Great Falls, MT 59405; 406-268-3701; jobs@gfcmsu.edu. GFC MSU’s Non-Discrimination Policy and Discrimination Grievance Procedures can be located on the GFC MSU Website: http://www.gfcmsu.edu/about/policies/400policies.html Great Falls College MSU is a tobacco-free campus. Smoking and the use of any tobacco products is not permitted on any College property. Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Transcript List of References License and Certification Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Human Resources Office 2100 16th Ave S Great Falls, MT 59405 406.268.3701 jobs@gfcmsu.edu accessibility | terms of use / privacy policy | your right to know To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.gfcmsu.edu/postings/2585": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty Pool - Music &amp; Art",
      "description": "Great Falls College Montana State University Employment Opportunities | Adjunct Faculty Pool - Music &amp; Art Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Benefits HR Office GFCMSU HOME Choose Great Falls Adjunct Faculty Pool - Music & Art Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applications to the Adjunct Faculty pool are kept on file for 24 months. After that time, you will be asked to update your application in order to keep the pool current. You can update your application materials at any time by signing back in to your account, keep your login and password information used for your initial application to the pool. Position Details Position Information Working Title Adjunct Faculty Pool - Music & Art Brief Position Overview Great Falls College MSU is seeking adjunct instructors for Music and Art courses within the Communication, Arts & Humanities Department. Adjunct faculty are hired on a semester-by-semester basis to meet instructional needs and may teach in-person, online, or hybrid courses. Qualified applicants must hold a master’s degree in the teaching field or a closely related discipline, with at least nine (9) graduate-level semester credits in the subject area to be taught. Faculty Tenure Track No Faculty Rank Adjunct Instructor Position Number Department Office of Academics Division Academics Appointment Type Faculty Contract Term Semester Semester If other, specify From date If other, specify End date FLSA Union Affiliation Not applicable (Temporary) FTE n/a Benefits Eligible No Compensation By Credit Salary $845.00 per credit for Academic (pay is different for clinical) Contract Type LOA If other, please specify Recruitment Type External Position Details General Statement Great Falls College is seeking enthusiastic and knowledgeable Adjunct Faculty in Music and Art to join our Communication, Arts & Humanities Department. Whether your expertise is in music history, music theory, drawing, design, painting, or another related area, this is an opportunity to bring your knowledge and creativity into the classroom and make a meaningful impact on our students. Adjunct opportunities may be available for in-person and online instruction with the potential to teach evening classes , depending on course needs and instructor qualifications. Candidates may be considered for one or multiple courses based on their education and areas of expertise. As an adjunct faculty member, you’ll create an engaging and supportive learning environment while helping students build their knowledge, skills, and appreciation for the arts. Responsibilities may include developing and delivering course content, facilitating classroom or online learning activities, evaluating student work, providing timely feedback, maintaining course records, communicating with students, and supporting the overall mission of Great Falls College. Duties and Responsibilities Prepare and teach subject matter content to traditional and nontraditional students. Prepare syllabi consistent with approved course outlines and department expectations. Utilize the College’s learning platform (Canvas) to deliver course content, maintain course materials, communicate with students, and track student progress. Maintain regular and timely communication with students, responding to inquiries and providing feedback in accordance with college and departmental expectations. Accurately report student attendance and participation as required by institutional policies and deadlines. Develop and administer assessments that effectively measure student learning outcomes and provide timely, constructive feedback on student work. Submit midterm and final grades, as well as other required academic records and reports, by established deadlines. Stay current in the field through ongoing professional development and engagement with discipline-specific trends and practices. Contribute to a positive and effective learning and work environment by interacting professionally and appropriately with students, colleagues, supervisors, and visitors. Required Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills Qualified applicants must hold a Master’s degree in the teaching field or a closely related discipline, with at least nine (9) graduate-level semester credits in the subject area to be taught. Preferred Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills Master’s or Doctorate degree(s) in industry or related field; Appropriate industry or field certifications (if applicable); Related work experience in degree area, industry or field of expertise; Successful teaching experience face to face and/or online; Experience in Higher Education, two-year college, or Community College setting. Computer literacy, including Microsoft Office Suite. The Successful Candidate Will Special Requirements This job description should not be construed as an exhaustive statement of duties, responsibilities or requirements, but as a general description of the job. Nothing contained herein restricts Montana State University’s rights to assign or reassign duties and responsibilities to this job at any time. Physical Demands To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. The requirements listed above are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. The Program Program Information can be found in the catalog here: http://www.gfcmsu.edu/programs/index.html Course Catalog can be found here: http://catalog.gfcmsu.edu/ The Department The College Great Falls College is a 2-year institution in the Montana University System, dedicated to providing high quality, affordable education. Located in the heart of Montana, we offer more than 25 academic programs that prepare students for immediate employment or seamless transfer to four-year institutions. Our small class sizes, 8- and 16-week courses, dedicated faculty and vibrant learning community ensure students receive the personalized attention and support needed to succeed. Our non-credit workforce training programs provide practical skills and knowledge for in-demand careers, helping students enter the workforce or advance their careers with confidence. At Great Falls College, we believe in making education accessible to everyone. Our tuition is among the most affordable in Montana, and we offer financial aid options, scholarships, and dual credit opportunities to help students save on their educational journey. Join the River Otter team and help transform lives and shape the future of our community. This position has supervisory duties? Posting Detail Information Announcement Number FAC - VA - 2700001P Number of Vacancies Varies Desired Start Date Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Close Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions Summary Applications to the Adjunct Faculty pool are kept on file for 24 months. After that time, you will be asked to update your application in order to keep the pool current. You can update your application materials at any time by signing back in to your account, keep your login and password information used for your initial application to the pool. Quick Link for Internal Postings https://jobs.gfcmsu.edu/postings/2575 Notices Great Falls College Montana State University is committed to providing a working and learning environment free from discrimination. As such, the College does not discriminate in the admission, access to or conduct of its educational programs and activities nor in its employment policies and practices on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, ethnicity, creed, service in the uniformed services (as defined in state and federal law), veteran status, gender, age, political beliefs, marital or family status, pregnancy, physical or mental disability, genetic information, gender identity, gender expression, or sexual orientation or preference. In support of the College’s mission to be inclusive and diverse, applications from qualified minorities, women, veterans and persons with disabilities are highly encouraged. Great Falls College Montana State University makes accommodation for any known disability that may interfere with an applicant’s ability to compete in the hiring process or an employee’s ability to perform the duties of the job. In compliance with the Montana Veteran’s Employment Preference Act, GFC MSU provides preference in employment to veterans, disabled veterans, and certain eligible relatives of veterans. To claim veteran’s preference or request accommodation, contact the Human Resources Office, Great Falls College Montana State University, 2100 16th Ave S, Great Falls, MT 59405; 406-268-3701; jobs@gfcmsu.edu. GFC MSU’s Non-Discrimination Policy and Discrimination Grievance Procedures can be located on the GFC MSU Website: http://www.gfcmsu.edu/about/policies/400policies.html Great Falls College MSU is a tobacco-free campus. Smoking and the use of any tobacco products is not permitted on any College property. Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Transcript List of References Optional Documents License and Certification Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Human Resources Office 2100 16th Ave S Great Falls, MT 59405 406.268.3701 jobs@gfcmsu.edu accessibility | terms of use / privacy policy | your right to know To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.gfcmsu.edu/postings/2561": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty Pool",
      "description": "Great Falls College Montana State University Employment Opportunities | Adjunct Faculty Pool Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Benefits HR Office GFCMSU HOME Choose Great Falls Adjunct Faculty Pool Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applications to the Adjunct Faculty pool are kept on file for 24 months. After that time, you will be asked to update your application in order to keep the pool current. You can update your application materials at any time by signing back in to your account, keep your login and password information used for your initial application to the pool. Position Details Position Information Working Title Adjunct Faculty Pool Brief Position Overview Great Falls College MSU has varying needs for adjunct instructors. Adjunct instructors are hired Semester to Semester based on the needs of the institution, in a variety of subject areas. Faculty Tenure Track No Faculty Rank Adjunct Instructor Position Number Department Office of Academics Division Academics Appointment Type Faculty Contract Term Semester Semester If other, specify From date If other, specify End date FLSA Union Affiliation Not applicable (Temporary) FTE n/a Benefits Eligible No Compensation By Credit Salary $830.00 per credit for Academic (pay is different for clinical) Contract Type LOA If other, please specify Recruitment Type External Position Details General Statement Adjunct instructors are hired based on the needs of the institution, which are evaluated every semester in each of these areas: General Education, Business, Technology & Transfer; Trades; and Health Sciences. In some instances, specific open adjunct positions will be advertised on our job seekers webpage. However, because our needs can change quickly and because we may not advertise an opening, having your application on file with us in an Adjunct Faculty pool may be beneficial! Duties and Responsibilities Preparing and teaching subject matter content to traditional and nontraditional students. Assist with syllabus preparation and developing curriculum. Ability to stay current in field. Contribute to an effective work atmosphere by interacting positively and appropriately with students, co-workers, supervisors and visitors. Required Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills Required qualifications for adjunct teaching positions vary depending on the type of openings available and are based on the Montana Board of Regent’s Policy 730. View the policy here: http://mus.edu/borpol/bor700/730.pdf Preferred Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills Master’s or Doctorate degree(s) in industry or related field; Appropriate industry or field certifications (if applicable); Related work experience in degree area, industry or field of expertise; Successful teaching experience face to face and/or online; Experience in Higher Education, two-year college, or Community College setting. Computer literacy, including Microsoft Office Suite. The Successful Candidate Will Special Requirements This job description should not be construed as an exhaustive statement of duties, responsibilities or requirements, but as a general description of the job. Nothing contained herein restricts Montana State University’s rights to assign or reassign duties and responsibilities to this job at any time. Physical Demands To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. The requirements listed above are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. The Program Program Information can be found in the catalog here: http://www.gfcmsu.edu/programs/index.html Course Catalog can be found here: http://catalog.gfcmsu.edu/ The Department The College Great Falls College is a 2-year institution in the Montana University System, dedicated to providing high quality, affordable education. Located in the heart of Montana, we offer more than 25 academic programs that prepare students for immediate employment or seamless transfer to four-year institutions. Our small class sizes, 8- and 16-week courses, dedicated faculty and vibrant learning community ensure students receive the personalized attention and support needed to succeed. Our non-credit workforce training programs provide practical skills and knowledge for in-demand careers, helping students enter the workforce or advance their careers with confidence. At Great Falls College, we believe in making education accessible to everyone. Our tuition is among the most affordable in Montana, and we offer financial aid options, scholarships, and dual credit opportunities to help students save on their educational journey. Join the River Otter team and help transform lives and shape the future of our community. This position has supervisory duties? Posting Detail Information Announcement Number FAC - VA - 2600001P Number of Vacancies Varies Desired Start Date Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Close Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions Summary Applications to the Adjunct Faculty pool are kept on file for 24 months. After that time, you will be asked to update your application in order to keep the pool current. You can update your application materials at any time by signing back in to your account, keep your login and password information used for your initial application to the pool. Quick Link for Internal Postings https://jobs.gfcmsu.edu/postings/2439 Notices Great Falls College Montana State University is committed to providing a working and learning environment free from discrimination. As such, the College does not discriminate in the admission, access to or conduct of its educational programs and activities nor in its employment policies and practices on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, ethnicity, creed, service in the uniformed services (as defined in state and federal law), veteran status, gender, age, political beliefs, marital or family status, pregnancy, physical or mental disability, genetic information, gender identity, gender expression, or sexual orientation or preference. In support of the College’s mission to be inclusive and diverse, applications from qualified minorities, women, veterans and persons with disabilities are highly encouraged. Great Falls College Montana State University makes accommodation for any known disability that may interfere with an applicant’s ability to compete in the hiring process or an employee’s ability to perform the duties of the job. In compliance with the Montana Veteran’s Employment Preference Act, GFC MSU provides preference in employment to veterans, disabled veterans, and certain eligible relatives of veterans. To claim veteran’s preference or request accommodation, contact the Human Resources Office, Great Falls College Montana State University, 2100 16th Ave S, Great Falls, MT 59405; 406-268-3701; jobs@gfcmsu.edu. GFC MSU’s Non-Discrimination Policy and Discrimination Grievance Procedures can be located on the GFC MSU Website: http://www.gfcmsu.edu/about/policies/400policies.html Great Falls College MSU is a tobacco-free campus. Smoking and the use of any tobacco products is not permitted on any College property. Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Transcript Optional Documents Curriculum Vitae License and Certification Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please indicate what subject area's you are interested in teaching here. (For example, Mathematics, Writing, Psychology, Lifelong Learning, etc.) (Open Ended Question) Human Resources Office 2100 16th Ave S Great Falls, MT 59405 406.268.3701 jobs@gfcmsu.edu accessibility | terms of use / privacy policy | your right to know To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
